# The site deploys from the REPOSITORY ROOT even though its Root Directory is
# `site`, because `npm run build` runs theme:check first and that reads
# design/palettes.json through tool/gen-theme.mjs — both one level above `site`.
# Everything listed here is Flutter source or build output the web build never
# reads.
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. Without it, gitignore
# syntax matches at any depth: a bare `assets/` would also drop site/assets/,
# which holds the three woff2 faces next/font inlines and the three TTFs satori
# needs for the share card. The build would succeed and the site would render in
# a fallback font.
/build/
/.dart_tool/
/android/
/ios/
/linux/
/macos/
/windows/
/web/
/test/
/assets/

# NOT /lib/. `theme:check` compares the GENERATED Dart palette against
# design/palettes.json, and that file lives at
# lib/core/theme/palettes/generated_palettes.dart. Excluding the directory made
# the check report it as stale on the build machine — correctly, since a missing
# file is not an up-to-date one — and the deploy failed with a message about
# uncommitted theme changes that were not actually uncommitted. 812 KB of Dart
# source is a cheap price for the guard that keeps the app and the site from
# drifting apart.
/.git/
node_modules/
/site/.next/
/site/out/
/site/.vercel/
